netfilter: ipset: let destroy callbacks adjust ext mem size

jira KERNEL-1930
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9
commit-author Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
commit 490937b88cb592cc0c5367758edd700fd5abd15c
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9/490937b8.failed

For bitmap this change makes no difference, because destructors are
called synchronously.

List type however calls them via call_rcu() so accounting decrement can
happen after list_set_flush() set ext_size to 0.

'set->elements = 0' can be removed for the same reason in the list type
case, it calls 'set->elements--' for each element.

Fixes: 9e41f26a505c ("netfilter: ipset: Count non-static extension memory for userspace")
	Suggested-by: Jozsef Kadlecsik <kadlec@netfilter.org>
	Signed-off-by: Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>
	Acked-by: Jozsef Kadlecsik <kadlec@netfilter.org>
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
(cherry picked from commit 490937b88cb592cc0c5367758edd700fd5abd15c)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_bitmap_gen.h
#	net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_list_set.c
diff --cc net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_bitmap_gen.h
index 293abd522caf,d6a7e6604542..000000000000
--- a/net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_bitmap_gen.h
+++ b/net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_bitmap_gen.h
@@@ -75,7 -77,7 +75,11 @@@ mtype_flush(struct ip_set *set
  		mtype_ext_cleanup(set);
  	bitmap_zero(map->members, map->elements);
  	set->elements = 0;
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	set->ext_size = 0;
++=======
+ 	DEBUG_NET_WARN_ON_ONCE(atomic64_read(&set->ext_size) > 0);
++>>>>>>> 490937b88cb5 (netfilter: ipset: let destroy callbacks adjust ext mem size)
  }
  
  /* Calculate the actual memory size of the set data */
diff --cc net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_list_set.c
index a10cda4d185c,f070088742d6..000000000000
--- a/net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_list_set.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/ipset/ip_set_list_set.c
@@@ -423,8 -423,7 +423,12 @@@ list_set_flush(struct ip_set *set
  
  	list_for_each_entry_safe(e, n, &map->members, list)
  		list_set_del(set, e);
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	set->elements = 0;
 +	set->ext_size = 0;
++=======
+ 	DEBUG_NET_WARN_ON_ONCE(set->elements > 0);
++>>>>>>> 490937b88cb5 (netfilter: ipset: let destroy callbacks adjust ext mem size)
  }
  
  static void
